C_A(Z) = \int_T \mathbf{1}\{ q(\tau, Z) \ge p(\tau) \}\, w(\tau)\, d\mu(\tau)

A.4 Adequacy Ratios

For each subsystem i, define required level X_i^{\text{req}} and critical level X_i^{\text{crit}} with 0 < X_i^{\text{crit}} < X_i^{\text{req}}.

Adequacy ratio:

r_i(Z) = \frac{X_i}{X_i^{\text{req}}}

Critical adequacy ratio:

r_i^{\text{crit}} = \frac{X_i^{\text{crit}}}{X_i^{\text{req}}}

A subsystem is critical-active if r_i > r_i^{\text{crit}}.

