Appendix F. Multi-Agent Verification Formalisms

F.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts

Let agent i have contract \mathcal{C}_i = (A_i, G_i), where A_i is the set of assumptions on inputs and G_i is the set of guarantees on outputs. The global property \mathcal{P} holds if:

\bigwedge_i \mathcal{C}_i \Rightarrow \mathcal{P}

under well-formed composition.

F.2 Compositional Verification

Theorem F.1 (Compositional Safety).
If each local contract \mathcal{C}_i is verified individually, and the composition satisfies the compatibility conditions, then the global safety property holds.

Proof. By induction on the number of agents. For n=1, trivial. For n>1, the composition of n-1 agents satisfies a derived contract by induction, and the addition of the nth agent preserves the property under the compatibility condition. ∎

