```text
Algorithm 2: Viability Kernel Approximation
Input: model parameters, policy set Π, acceptable set V, target failure probability ε
Output: viability kernel estimate K_ε

Generate initial state samples {Z0^j} from distribution μ0
for each sample:
    for each policy π in Π:
        simulate many trajectories under π
        estimate P_π(Z0) = fraction staying in V
    if max_π P_π(Z0) >= 1 - ε:
        label Z0 as viable
    else:
        label Z0 as nonviable
Train neural network Nθ to classify viable vs nonviable states
