Appendix K. Open Problems and Future Work

The formal theory identifies several open problems:

1. Existence of global viability kernel in high dimensions — requires extensions of viability theory to non-Markovian stochastic delays.
2. Estimation of task reliability functions q(τ,Z) — requires a standardized benchmark suite for civilization-critical tasks.
3. Calibration of coupling coefficients — requires longitudinal data on energy, compute, and institutional adaptation.
4. Formal verification of multi-agent contracts under partial observability — current assume-guarantee methods assume complete knowledge of contracts.
5. Endogenization of geopolitical fragmentation F_t — currently treated as exogenous; a game-theoretic extension is needed.
6. Integration with climate and biosphere models — the current state vector omits planetary boundary variables.

These problems define the next research frontier.

